# App‑X Terraform

Infrastructure as Code for Deploying an EKS Cluster on AWS

This project uses Terraform to provision and manage an Amazon EKS (Elastic Kubernetes Service) cluster and its supporting AWS infrastructure.

The **app‑x‑terraform** project automates deployment of a scalable EKS environment, including:

- VPC with public and private subnets  
- EKS cluster with managed node groups  
- Application Load Balancer (ALB)  
- DynamoDB for data persistence  
- GitHub Actions for CI/CD automation  

